window.REVIEW_DETAILS["ny_b1-a79f1f8237fec3cc"]={"key":"ny_b1-a79f1f8237fec3cc","group":"ny_b1","uid":"a79f1f8237fec3cc","rank":22,"title":"willowmere oee cell12 extension","occupation":"industrial_engineers","archetype":"code_exec","subbatch":"corpus_b1","prompt":"You are the industrial engineer supporting manufacturing analytics at Willowmere Laboratories. Imani Petrosyan needs the corporate OEE feed ready before Cell 12 enters production in September, but the reporting code was left behind by a contractor and has no explanation of its unusual decisions. The current implementation is attached as `legacy_oee.py`; it runs reliably for Cells 1–11 and remains the acceptance baseline for those cells. The supporting operational and commissioning evidence is in `cell12_evidence.md`, including the Ironvale Provisions equipment details and the plant practices that may explain why the legacy code omits two downtime reasons, places the third-shift boundary eleven minutes away from the nominal handover, and treats one existing cell differently. Extend the tool without changing the results or output contract for Cells 1–11, and add Cell 12 using the interpretation you can best defend from the supplied evidence. The importable entry point must be `build_report(events, period_start, period_end)` and must accept the same event schema, period values, and return structure demonstrated by `legacy_oee.py`, with Cell 12 added in the established cell and shift ordering. Also provide a command-line interface invoked as `python oee_report.py INPUT.json OUTPUT.json`; the input object contains `events`, `period_start`, and `period_end`, and the output must be the JSON representation of the function result. Any event whose `duration_minutes` is zero or negative must be rejected with `ValueError` rather than ignored, corrected, or included, and invalid command-line input must produce a clear error and a nonzero exit status. Repeated runs on identical input must return structurally identical results and write byte-identical JSON. Include `LOGIC_RECONSTRUCTION.md` with a concise account of what the three unusual legacy behaviors do, the operational reason supported for each, your Cell 12 recommendation and alternatives considered, and enough usage, assumptions, limitations, and reproduction information for Noor Calderon to maintain the feed. Use Python 3.11 with only the standard library and pandas, without network access. Package `oee_report.py` and `LOGIC_RECONSTRUCTION.md` inside `willowmere_oee_extension.zip`, and write that single deliverable at the top level of the working directory using exactly that filename.\n\n---\n\nThe files referred to above are in `references/`:\n\n- `references/legacy_oee.py` — Executable acceptance baseline defining the existing event schema, report structure, metric calculations, cell ordering, shift assignment, downtime treatment, and special handling for Cells 1–11.\n- `references/cell12_evidence.md` — Operational notes and Cell 12 commissioning evidence supporting reconstruction of the legacy exceptions and the choice of reporting treatment for the new cell.\n\nWrite your finished work to the **top level of the current working directory**, using exactly these filenames:\n\n- `willowmere_oee_extension.zip` — Executable Cell 12 OEE reporting extension and its written logic reconstruction. (The archive must contain `oee_report.py` and `LOGIC_RECONSTRUCTION.md`. The Python module must expose `build_report(events, period_start, period_end)` and the documented command-line interface, run offline under Python 3.11, and use no dependencies beyond the standard library and pandas.)\n\nNothing outside those filenames is collected. A correct file written anywhere else, or under any other name, scores zero.\n","inputs":[{"name":"package/public/reference_files/cell12_evidence.md","bytes":1103,"extension":".md","url":"assets/64863f8314a1fe4046dc1bc4cb671b0c0726e66f37a9a447b145ea66b267559a.md","sha256":"64863f8314a1fe4046dc1bc4cb671b0c0726e66f37a9a447b145ea66b267559a","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"# Cell 12 commissioning notes\n\nWillowmere's OEE dashboard has two intentional omissions in the downtime feed. `PM` is scheduled preventive maintenance performed outside the OEE loading window, and `NO_MATERIAL` is material starvation owned by the upstream supply process. Neither is treated as production-window loss in the established leadership metric.\n\nThe night-shift report changes at the MES release marker 21:49. The physical handover starts at 22:00, but the eleven-minute controlled transfer is attributed to the outgoing second shift in historical leadership reporting.\n\nCELL07 is a twin-spindle Ironvale Provisions machine. One completed machine cycle releases two bearings through the paired discharge. The commissioned CELL12 uses the same twin-spindle equipment family and paired discharge arrangement. Its ideal cycle is 18 seconds per completed paired-output cycle.\n\nOperations considered treating Cell 12 as a normal single-output cell or extending the paired-output treatment. The September production date is fixed; the corporate feed must be ready before the cell enters production.\n","truncated":false}},{"name":"package/public/reference_files/legacy_oee.py","bytes":4357,"extension":".py","url":"assets/6a180c1505b8a4cec7966428d35b874326993a4d522a6a2bbc85ac8b6473f6cf.py","sha256":"6a180c1505b8a4cec7966428d35b874326993a4d522a6a2bbc85ac8b6473f6cf","preview":{"kind":"text","text":"\"\"\"Reference OEE implementation used by the Willowmere plant feed.\"\"\"\nfrom datetime import datetime, time\n\nCELL_CONFIG = {\n    \"CELL01\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 12.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n    \"CELL02\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 15.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n    \"CELL03\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 10.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n    \"CELL04\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 20.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n    \"CELL05\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 18.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n    \"CELL06\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 16.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n    \"CELL07\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 24.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 2},\n    \"CELL08\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 14.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n    \"CELL09\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 22.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n    \"CELL10\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 11.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n    \"CELL11\": {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 19.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1},\n}\nSHIFT_ORDER = (\"SHIFT1\", \"SHIFT2\", \"SHIFT3\")\nEXCLUDED_REASONS = {\"PM\", \"NO_MATERIAL\"}\n\ndef _ts(value):\n    return datetime.fromisoformat(value)\n\ndef _shift(value):\n    t = value.time()\n    if time(6, 0) \u003c= t \u003c time(14, 0):\n        return \"SHIFT1\"\n    if time(14, 0) \u003c= t \u003c time(21, 49):\n        return \"SHIFT2\"\n    return \"SHIFT3\"\n\ndef _metrics(run, down, good, reject, cfg):\n    planned = run + down\n    produced = good + reject\n    theoretical = produced / cfg[\"outputs_per_cycle\"] * cfg[\"ideal_cycle_seconds\"] / 60.0\n    availability = run / planned if planned > 0 else None\n    performance = min(1.0, theoretical / run) if run > 0 else None\n    quality = good / produced if produced > 0 else None\n    oee = availability * performance * quality if None not in (availability, performance, quality) else None\n    return {\"run_minutes\": run, \"downtime_minutes\": down, \"planned_production_minutes\": planned,\n            \"good_units\": good, \"reject_units\": reject, \"theoretical_production_minutes\": theoretical,\n            \"availability\": availability, \"performance\": performance, \"quality\": quality, \"oee\": oee}\n\ndef build_report(events, period_start, period_end):\n    start, end = _ts(period_start), _ts(period_end)\n    buckets = {cell: {shift: [0.0, 0.0, 0, 0] for shift in SHIFT_ORDER} for cell in CELL_CONFIG}\n    for event in events:\n        duration = float(event[\"duration_minutes\"])\n        # Legacy baseline assumes positive durations; extension adds explicit validation.\n        stamp = _ts(event[\"timestamp\"])\n        if stamp \u003c start or stamp >= end or event[\"cell_id\"] not in buckets:\n            continue\n        cell, shift = event[\"cell_id\"], _shift(stamp)\n        state = event.get(\"state\")\n        if state == \"RUN\":\n            b = buckets[cell][shift]\n            b[0] += duration; b[2] += int(event.get(\"good_units\", 0) or 0); b[3] += int(event.get(\"reject_units\", 0) or 0)\n        elif state == \"DOWN\" and event.get(\"downtime_reason\") not in EXCLUDED_REASONS:\n            buckets[cell][shift][1] += duration\n    cells = []\n    plant_raw = [0.0, 0.0, 0, 0]\n    plant_theoretical = 0.0\n    for cell, cfg in CELL_CONFIG.items():\n        shifts = []\n        cell_raw = [0.0, 0.0, 0, 0]\n        for shift in SHIFT_ORDER:\n            run, down, good, reject = buckets[cell][shift]\n            m = _metrics(run, down, good, reject, cfg)\n            shifts.append({\"shift_id\": shift, **m})\n            cell_raw[0] += run; cell_raw[1] += down; cell_raw[2] += good; cell_raw[3] += reject\n        agg = _metrics(*cell_raw, cfg)\n        cells.append({\"cell_id\": cell, \"shifts\": shifts, \"aggregate\": agg})\n        plant_raw[0] += cell_raw[0]; plant_raw[1] += cell_raw[1]; plant_raw[2] += cell_raw[2]; plant_raw[3] += cell_raw[3]\n        plant_theoretical += agg[\"theoretical_production_minutes\"]\n    plant = _metrics(*plant_raw, {\"ideal_cycle_seconds\": 0.0, \"outputs_per_cycle\": 1})\n    plant[\"theoretical_production_minutes\"] = plant_theoretical\n    plant[\"performance\"] = min(1.0, plant_theoretical / plant_raw[0]) if plant_raw[0] > 0 else None\n    plant[\"oee\"] = plant[\"availability\"] * plant[\"performance\"] * plant[\"quality\"] if None not in (plant[\"availability\"], plant[\"performance\"], plant[\"quality\"]) else None\n    return {\"period_start\": period_start, \"period_end\": period_end, \"cells\": cells, \"plant\": plant}\n\nif __name__ == \"__main__\":\n    import json, sys\n    print(json.dumps(build_report([], \"2026-01-01T00:00:00\", \"2026-01-02T00:00:00\"), indent=2))\n","truncated":false}}],"gold":[{"name":"package/private/gold/willowmere_oee_extension.zip","bytes":4327,"extension":".zip","url":"assets/ac83ebefc6a489b27074aaba825bbedaccd718d1025284d22289d0239dec27cc.zip","sha256":"ac83ebefc6a489b27074aaba825bbedaccd718d1025284d22289d0239dec27cc","preview":{"kind":"unavailable","note":"此格式未做网页解析，原文件可下载。"}}],"rubric":[{"rubric_item_id":"R01","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Calling `build_report` with a valid event collection and valid period values returns the report object rather than printing it, terminating the process, or requiring global input.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Imported module exercised by hidden tests.","grader_hint":"Extract the submitted archive, import the implementation in a clean Python 3.11 process, call the entry point with a minimal valid fixture, and inspect the returned object."},{"rubric_item_id":"R02","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The returned object conforms to the legacy report's nested keys, value types, and cell/shift structure, extended only as needed to represent Cell 12.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Return value from schema-focused hidden fixtures.","grader_hint":"Recursively compare the result schema with the reference implementation's schema and verify that the extension does not rename or remove established fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"R03","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report identifies the requested `period_start` and `period_end` using the same representation as the legacy implementation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Period fields in hidden-test output.","grader_hint":"Use non-default period values and compare the relevant output fields to the legacy baseline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R04","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The report emits Cells 1–12 exactly once each in the established ascending cell order.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cell collection returned for a valid fixture.","grader_hint":"Inspect cell identifiers and ordering, including a fixture in which some cells have no events."},{"rubric_item_id":"R05","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Every cell emits all established shift records in the legacy shift order, including shifts with no eligible activity.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Per-cell shift collections in sparse hidden fixtures.","grader_hint":"Use events for only one shift and verify the complete ordered shift structure against the baseline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R06","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For ordinary valid Cell 1–11 inputs, all non-Cell-12 report values equal the legacy implementation's values, with numeric differences no greater than ±1e-9.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Differential hidden tests against `legacy_oee.py`.","grader_hint":"Generate representative single-cell fixtures across Cells 1–11 and recursively compare all established output fields."},{"rubric_item_id":"R07","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"For a mixed fixture containing all legacy cells and all shifts, the complete Cells 1–11 portion remains equal to the legacy result within ±1e-9 for numeric values.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Mixed-load differential hidden test.","grader_hint":"Compare a fixture containing run, downtime, good, and reject activity across all legacy cells; this checks that adding Cell 12 did not alter shared aggregation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R08","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event starting exactly at `period_start` is included according to the legacy half-open period convention.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Start-boundary hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Place one otherwise eligible event exactly at the start and compare its contribution with the reference result."},{"rubric_item_id":"R09","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event starting exactly at `period_end` is excluded according to the legacy half-open period convention.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"End-boundary hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Place one event exactly at the end and verify that no duration or units from it enter the report."},{"rubric_item_id":"R10","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event before the requested period does not contribute to cell, shift, or plant aggregates.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pre-period hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Pair an in-period event with a pre-period event and compare the output with the in-period event alone."},{"rubric_item_id":"R11","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event after the requested period does not contribute to cell, shift, or plant aggregates.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Post-period hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Pair an in-period event with a post-period event and confirm that aggregates are unchanged."},{"rubric_item_id":"R12","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event beginning immediately before 06:00 is assigned to third shift as in the legacy implementation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Shift-boundary hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use a timestamp one second before 06:00 and inspect which shift receives its duration and units."},{"rubric_item_id":"R13","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event beginning exactly at 06:00 is assigned to first shift.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exact 06:00 hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Verify the contribution appears in first shift and not third shift."},{"rubric_item_id":"R14","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event beginning immediately before 14:00 is assigned to first shift.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pre-14:00 hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use a timestamp one second before 14:00 and inspect shift totals."},{"rubric_item_id":"R15","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event beginning exactly at 14:00 is assigned to second shift.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exact 14:00 hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Verify the event contributes only to second shift."},{"rubric_item_id":"R16","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event beginning immediately before the legacy 21:49 third-shift boundary remains in second shift.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Pre-21:49 hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use 21:48:59 local plant time and inspect the shift allocation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R17","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"An event beginning exactly at 21:49 is assigned to third shift.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Exact 21:49 hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Verify that the event's duration and units appear in third shift rather than second shift."},{"rubric_item_id":"R18","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Downtime carrying the legacy `PM` reason is removed from planned-production and downtime contributions exactly as in the baseline.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Single-reason hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Compare otherwise identical reports with and without a `PM` downtime event; use the reference implementation to check every affected aggregate."},{"rubric_item_id":"R19","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Downtime carrying the legacy `NO_MATERIAL` reason is removed from planned-production and downtime contributions exactly as in the baseline.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Single-reason hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Exercise `NO_MATERIAL` independently of `PM` and compare all affected metrics with the reference implementation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R20","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A downtime event with an ordinary reason code remains included in the applicable planned-production and downtime aggregates.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Ordinary-downtime hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use a non-excluded code from the supplied evidence and verify its duration changes the same fields as in the baseline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R21","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A downtime event with a missing reason follows the legacy included-downtime behavior rather than being silently dropped.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Null-reason hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use the schema's null reason representation and compare its treatment to the reference implementation."},{"rubric_item_id":"R22","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Included run durations are summed into run minutes for the correct cell and shift within ±1e-9 minute.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Multiple-run-event hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use distinct fractional durations in one cell and shift and compare the sum to the returned run value."},{"rubric_item_id":"R23","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Included downtime durations are summed into downtime minutes for the correct cell and shift within ±1e-9 minute.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Multiple-downtime-event hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use multiple non-excluded downtime rows with fractional durations and verify the resulting total."},{"rubric_item_id":"R24","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Planned-production minutes preserve the legacy relationship to included run and downtime minutes within ±1e-9 minute.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Mixed-state hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Check the returned planned-production value against the corresponding run and included-downtime components and against the legacy output."},{"rubric_item_id":"R25","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Good-unit quantities from eligible production events aggregate to the correct cell, shift, and plant values.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Distinct-quantity hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use unique good-unit counts across cells and shifts so incorrect grouping is observable."},{"rubric_item_id":"R26","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Reject-unit quantities from eligible production events aggregate to the correct cell, shift, and plant values.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Distinct-reject hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use unique reject counts and verify each aggregation level independently."},{"rubric_item_id":"R27","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A standard legacy cell applies its configured ideal-cycle value and one-unit-per-cycle treatment when calculating performance, within ±1e-9.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Standard-cell performance fixture.","grader_hint":"Choose a non-special legacy cell, compute performance from its supplied configuration, and compare with the output."},{"rubric_item_id":"R28","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The special existing cell applies the paired-output branch reconstructed from the legacy code, producing performance within ±1e-9 of the baseline.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Special-cell performance fixture.","grader_hint":"Use a fixture where treating every bearing as a separate machine cycle would visibly differ from the paired-output result."},{"rubric_item_id":"R29","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Cell 12 uses the commissioned ideal-cycle value stated in the operational evidence, producing the expected theoretical production time within ±1e-9 minute.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cell 12 cycle-time hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Compute theoretical time from the Cell 12 commissioning value and compare it with the submitted result."},{"rubric_item_id":"R30","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Cell 12 applies the evidence-supported paired-output treatment rather than the standard single-output cell branch.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Cell 12 paired-output hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Choose a Cell 12 quantity for which paired and single-output formulas give different performance values and compare against the reference solution."},{"rubric_item_id":"R31","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Availability equals run minutes divided by planned-production minutes wherever that denominator is positive, within ±1e-9.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Positive-denominator metric fixtures.","grader_hint":"Recalculate availability from returned components for multiple cells and shifts."},{"rubric_item_id":"R32","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Performance equals the applicable theoretical production time divided by run time, subject to the legacy cap, within ±1e-9.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Uncapped performance fixtures.","grader_hint":"Use fixtures below the cap for standard, special, and Cell 12 equipment and compare recalculated ratios."},{"rubric_item_id":"R33","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Performance values that would exceed 1.0 are capped at exactly 1.0 as in the legacy implementation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Over-speed hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Provide enough units in a short run interval to exceed the uncapped ratio and inspect the returned performance."},{"rubric_item_id":"R34","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Quality equals good units divided by total produced units wherever production is positive, within ±1e-9.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Good-and-reject hidden fixtures.","grader_hint":"Use nontrivial good and reject counts and recompute the ratio from returned quantities."},{"rubric_item_id":"R35","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"OEE equals availability multiplied by performance and quality wherever all three factors are defined, within ±1e-9.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Complete-metric hidden fixtures.","grader_hint":"Recalculate OEE from the returned factors at shift, cell, and plant levels."},{"rubric_item_id":"R36","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A cell-shift with no planned-production minutes uses the same undefined-value representation as the legacy report for availability and dependent OEE.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Empty and fully excluded shift fixtures.","grader_hint":"Test both a genuinely empty shift and a shift containing only excluded downtime, then compare with the baseline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R37","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A cell-shift with no run minutes uses the legacy undefined-value representation for performance and dependent OEE.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Downtime-only hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use included downtime without run activity and compare all metric fields to the baseline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R38","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"A cell-shift with zero total produced units uses the legacy undefined-value representation for quality and dependent OEE.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Zero-production hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use positive run time with zero good and reject units and compare with the baseline."},{"rubric_item_id":"R39","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Plant run, downtime, planned-production, good-unit, and reject-unit totals equal the sums of their eligible cell contributions within ±1e-9 for minute values.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Multi-cell plant-aggregation fixture.","grader_hint":"Recalculate each plant component from the returned cell data, including Cell 12."},{"rubric_item_id":"R40","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Plant performance is calculated from aggregated theoretical production time and aggregated run time, including paired-output treatment, rather than by averaging cell performance percentages.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Unequal-cell-weight hidden fixture.","grader_hint":"Use cells with materially different run times and include a paired-output cell so a simple arithmetic average cannot match."},{"rubric_item_id":"R41","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Plant availability, quality, and OEE use the legacy weighted aggregate relationships rather than unweighted averages, each within ±1e-9.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Unequal-volume plant fixture.","grader_hint":"Recompute metrics from plant component totals and contrast them with arithmetic means of cell metrics."},{"rubric_item_id":"R42","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Any event whose `duration_minutes` is zero or negative causes `build_report` to raise `ValueError` before returning a report.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Zero-duration and negative-duration hidden fixtures.","grader_hint":"Test zero and at least two negative numeric values in otherwise valid events; reject both rather than allowing coercion or omission."},{"rubric_item_id":"R43","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Repeated calls to `build_report` with the same input produce deeply equal output without dependence on prior calls.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Repeated-call hidden test in one process and fresh processes.","grader_hint":"Call the function repeatedly, including after processing a different fixture, and compare the complete return objects."},{"rubric_item_id":"R44","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The implementation does not mutate the supplied event collection or its nested event mappings.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Before-and-after snapshots of hidden input.","grader_hint":"Deep-copy the fixture before invocation and compare it to the original object afterward."},{"rubric_item_id":"R45","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"The command-line interface processes a valid input object and writes a JSON report structurally equal to the direct `build_report` result.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Subprocess execution with a temporary input and output location.","grader_hint":"Run the documented command in Python 3.11, parse the output JSON, and compare it recursively with a direct function call."},{"rubric_item_id":"R46","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Two command-line runs on identical input write byte-identical JSON output.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Hashes of output from repeated subprocess runs.","grader_hint":"Run in fresh processes with separate output paths and compare raw bytes, not only parsed objects."},{"rubric_item_id":"R47","check":"execution","category":"deterministic","criterion":"Invalid command-line input, including an event with nonpositive duration, produces a clear diagnostic and a nonzero exit status without writing a valid-looking report.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Subprocess error-path hidden fixtures.","grader_hint":"Capture exit status, standard error, and output-path contents for malformed input and nonpositive duration cases."},{"rubric_item_id":"R48","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The written reconstruction accurately distinguishes the observed behavior of the two downtime exclusions, the shifted third-shift boundary, and the special-cell branch from the operational reasons supported by the evidence.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted logic reconstruction evaluated alongside the two supplied references.","grader_hint":"Confirm that all three behaviors are described correctly, explanations trace to supplied facts, and any inference is labeled rather than presented as certain."},{"rubric_item_id":"R49","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The Cell 12 recommendation compares the plausible standard-cell and paired-output treatments and justifies the selected treatment using commissioning evidence and its effect on OEE interpretation.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Recommendation section of the submitted reconstruction and executable Cell 12 behavior.","grader_hint":"Look for an explicit tradeoff, evidence from the Ironvale equipment description, and agreement between the recommendation and the implemented behavior."},{"rubric_item_id":"R50","check":"judge","category":"semantic","criterion":"The package is safely maintainable: operating assumptions and equipment parameters can be changed in one clear place, and the written account gives accurate offline reproduction steps, input expectations, limitations, and error behavior.","weight":2.0,"polarity":"credit","scaffolding":false,"cross_deliverable":false,"required":false,"evidence":"Submitted source and logic reconstruction.","grader_hint":"Review whether a maintainer could update a shift boundary, excluded-reason set, or cell equipment parameter without coordinated edits throughout the code, then follow the documented function and CLI reproduction guidance."}],"spec":{"professional_context":"Willowmere Laboratories relies on a stable plant OEE feed whose undocumented legacy exceptions already influence trusted leadership metrics. The industrial engineer must preserve established reporting for eleven cells while recommending and implementing defensible treatment for a newly commissioned twelfth cell.","difficulty_sources":["Reconstructing the intent of stable but undocumented OEE exceptions from executable behavior and operational evidence.","Preserving exact legacy outputs while extending shared plant aggregation to a new equipment configuration.","Choosing between standard and paired-output treatment for Cell 12 and explaining the metric consequence.","Maintaining deterministic function and command-line behavior with explicit invalid-duration rejection."],"authoring_plan":{"reference_materials":{"legacy_oee.py":{"role":"Provide a clean, executable Python 3.11 baseline for Cells 1–11 with no explanatory comments for the three unusual behaviors.","public_interface":"Expose `build_report(events, period_start, period_end)` and include a small executable demonstration that reveals the accepted Python types and returned JSON-compatible structure.","event_contract":{"fields":["event_id","cell_id","timestamp","duration_minutes","state","good_units","reject_units","downtime_reason"],"domain":"Cell identifiers are `CELL01` through `CELL11`; timestamps are ISO-8601 timezone-naive local plant times; state is `RUN` or `DOWN`; durations are numeric minutes; quantities are nonnegative integers; downtime reason is a string or null."},"report_contract":"Return period fields, an ascending list of cell records, three ordered shift records per cell, cell aggregates, and a plant aggregate. Metric fields are JSON-compatible floats or null under the baseline's zero-denominator rules.","behaviors":["Select events by event start timestamp using the half-open interval `[period_start, period_end)`.","Assign first shift from 06:00 inclusive to 14:00 exclusive.","Assign second shift from 14:00 inclusive to 21:49 exclusive.","Assign third shift from 21:49 inclusive through the overnight interval ending at 06:00 exclusive.","Exclude `PM` and `NO_MATERIAL` downtime from planned-production and downtime minutes; include ordinary and null downtime reasons.","Sum RUN duration as run minutes, included DOWN duration as downtime minutes, and their sum as planned-production minutes.","Aggregate good and reject units from eligible RUN events.","Use per-cell ideal-cycle constants for Cells 1–11.","Treat CELL07 as producing two bearings per machine cycle; all other legacy cells produce one bearing per cycle.","Availability is run divided by planned-production minutes.","Performance is theoretical production minutes divided by run minutes and is capped at 1.0.","Quality is good divided by good plus reject units.","OEE is availability times performance times quality.","Use null for a metric whose denominator is zero and for dependent OEE.","Compute plant metrics from aggregated components and theoretical time, not arithmetic means.","Always return all configured legacy cells and all shifts in deterministic order."]},"cell12_evidence.md":{"role":"Supply complete, mutually consistent workplace evidence for reconstructing intent and selecting Cell 12 treatment without directly prescribing implementation steps.","facts_to_include":["The two omitted reasons correspond to scheduled preventive maintenance outside the OEE loading window and material starvation owned by the upstream supply process.","The dashboard's night-shift attribution uses a 21:49 MES release marker because the physical handover begins at 22:00 after an eleven-minute controlled transfer; historical leadership reporting follows the release marker.","CELL07 uses a twin-spindle Ironvale machine that releases two bearings per completed machine cycle.","CELL12 is commissioned with the same twin-spindle equipment family and paired discharge arrangement as CELL07.","CELL12's ideal cycle is 18 seconds per completed paired-output cycle.","The commissioning options considered by operations are treating Cell 12 as a normal single-output cell or extending the paired-output equipment treatment.","The September production date and stakeholder need are stable facts."]}},"reference_solution":{"archive_members":["oee_report.py","LOGIC_RECONSTRUCTION.md"],"entrypoint":"build_report(events, period_start, period_end)","cli":"python oee_report.py INPUT.json OUTPUT.json","extension_behavior":["Preserve every legacy behavior for Cells 1–11.","Add CELL12 after CELL11 and emit the same three-shift and aggregate structure.","Apply CELL12's 18-second ideal cycle and two-bearings-per-cycle paired-output treatment.","Include CELL12 in plant component totals and theoretical production time.","Validate all selected and unselected input events before aggregation so any zero or negative `duration_minutes` raises `ValueError` and no report is returned.","Produce deterministic objects and canonical deterministic JSON using stable record order and fixed serialization settings.","Do not mutate caller-owned inputs.","On invalid CLI input, emit a concise field-specific diagnostic to standard error, return a nonzero status, and avoid leaving a valid-looking completed output."],"written_account":["Describe the observable effect of each excluded reason code and tie each to its operational ownership or loading-window basis.","Describe the exact 21:49 boundary and distinguish MES reporting attribution from the 22:00 physical handover.","Describe the CELL07 paired-output branch and why omitting it would overstate theoretical production.","Compare standard and paired-output treatments for CELL12, recommend paired output, and state the metric distortion caused by the rejected option.","Label claims as observed behavior, supplied fact, or inference where appropriate.","Document function and CLI use, input expectations, output interpretation, nonpositive-duration rejection, offline reproduction, deterministic behavior, and the timezone-naive limitation."],"maintainability":"Centralize shift boundaries, excluded reason codes, and per-cell equipment parameters so each assumption has one authoritative definition."},"hidden_tests":{"environment":{"python":"3.11","allowed_dependencies":["Python standard library","pandas"],"network":"forbidden","randomness":"none"},"strategy":["Extract the archive and import the submitted module in isolated temporary directories.","Use differential tests against the supplied legacy implementation for Cells 1–11, including single-cell, all-cell, sparse, mixed-state, and zero-denominator fixtures.","Use explicit boundary fixtures at period start, period end, 06:00, 14:00, and 21:49, plus one second before each shift boundary.","Exercise `PM`, `NO_MATERIAL`, ordinary, and null downtime reasons independently.","Use quantities and durations chosen to distinguish single-output from paired-output performance for CELL07 and CELL12.","Test performance both below and above the 1.0 cap.","Use unequal cell run times and volumes to distinguish weighted plant aggregation from arithmetic averaging.","Test zero and negative durations through both the importable function and CLI.","Run repeated calls in one interpreter, calls after unrelated fixtures, and CLI calls in fresh processes to verify determinism and absence of retained state.","Snapshot nested input structures before invocation to detect mutation.","Compare CLI JSON bytes across runs and parsed CLI output against direct function output."],"numeric_tolerances":{"minutes":"±1e-9 minute","ratios":"±1e-9","integer_counts":"exact"},"naive_solution_failures":["Merely adding CELL12 to the standard per-cell constants fails paired-output performance tests.","Replacing 21:49 with the nominal 22:00 handover fails boundary and legacy-parity tests.","Counting all downtime reasons fails exclusion and metric tests.","Averaging cell OEE values fails weighted plant aggregation tests.","Sorting only some report levels or using default JSON formatting inconsistently fails deterministic byte-output tests.","Silently dropping zero-duration rows fails explicit rejection tests."]},"verification":"Build the reference package, run every hidden fixture against it in clean Python 3.11 processes, confirm all execution predicates and numeric tolerances pass, then have a manufacturing-analytics reviewer verify that the written reconstruction is fully supported by the supplied evidence and agrees with the implementation."},"design_constraints":{"artifact_scope":"multi_artifact_bundle","structure":"strict_schema"},"reference_files":[{"artifact_id":"legacy_oee_implementation","filename":"legacy_oee.py","purpose":"Executable acceptance baseline defining the existing event schema, report structure, metric calculations, cell ordering, shift assignment, downtime treatment, and special handling for Cells 1–11.","required":true,"discovery":"Read and run this module to characterize the established reporting behavior that must remain unchanged."},{"artifact_id":"cell12_operational_evidence","filename":"cell12_evidence.md","purpose":"Operational notes and Cell 12 commissioning evidence supporting reconstruction of the legacy exceptions and the choice of reporting treatment for the new cell.","required":true,"discovery":"Use this evidence to distinguish supported explanations from inference and to decide which existing equipment logic applies to Cell 12."}],"deliverables":[{"deliverable_id":"extended_oee_reporting_package","filename":"willowmere_oee_extension.zip","media_type":"application/zip","description":"Executable Cell 12 OEE reporting extension and its written logic reconstruction.","required":true,"constraints":["The archive must contain `oee_report.py` and `LOGIC_RECONSTRUCTION.md`. The Python module must expose `build_report(events, period_start, period_end)` and the documented command-line interface, run offline under Python 3.11, and use no dependencies beyond the standard library and pandas."],"rendering_required":false}],"work_activity":"analyze_data","work_product":"engineering_package","internet_policy":"forbidden","evidence_policy":"closed_world_with_assumptions"},"source_metadata":{"prompt_version":"code_exec@v4","occupation":"industrial_engineers","sector":"manufacturing","task_archetype":"code_exec","estimated_professional_hours":7.0,"gold_policy_self_report_not_verified":{"author_type":"hybrid","reviewer_policy":"A reference script supplies the execution oracle for legacy parity and the fully specified Cell 12 extension; an independent manufacturing-analytics reviewer evaluates the reconstruction, recommendation, and maintainability criteria.","minimum_reviewers":2,"known_limitations":["The event model uses timezone-naive local plant timestamps and does not test daylight-saving transitions.","The hidden fixtures evaluate only the event fields and operating conventions demonstrated in the supplied legacy implementation.","Operational intent is judged against the supplied evidence bundle rather than external historical knowledge."],"reference_solution_passed_rubric":true}},"validation":{"label":"成品包存在","detail":"按公开题面存在纳入抽样；不视为内容正确性验收。","formal":false,"release_ready_recorded":true,"checks":[{"check":"package_integrity","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"},{"check":"gold_isolation","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"},{"check":"artifact_format","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":true,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"},{"check":"rendering","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":true,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"},{"check":"instruction_rubric_overlap","validator":"gdpval-package","validator_version":"v1","passed":false,"required":false,"metrics":{},"evidence_artifact_ids":[],"detail":"instruction 与 rubric criterion 存在 8-gram 逐字重叠: ['R42']","checked_at":"2026-08-20T19:05:16+00:00"}]},"source_path":"/inspire/hdd2/project/special-project-1/public/ynan/gdpval_data/corpus_b1/runs/a79f1f8237fec3cc","declared_deliverables":["willowmere_oee_extension.zip"]};
